.TH NMCRCON 1 "2026-09-26" "nmcrcon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nmcrcon \- Minecraft RCON client with an interactive shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nmcrcon
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
[\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]]
[\fICOMMAND\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nmcrcon
connects to a Minecraft RCON server and either starts an interactive shell or
executes commands non-interactively.
.PP
Each positional
.I COMMAND
argument is treated as one command. Use shell quoting to include spaces inside a
single command. When standard input is not a terminal,
.B nmcrcon
reads commands line-by-line from standard input. Blank lines and lines beginning
with
.B #
are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-host=\fIHOST\fR
Server host.
.TP
.B \-P, \-\-port=\fIPORT\fR
Server port.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-pass=\fIPASSWORD\fR
RCON password.
.TP
.B \-q, \-s, \-\-quiet, \-\-silent
Suppress command output.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print connection and execution details.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-wait=\fISECONDS\fR
Wait between queued commands and scripted commands.
.TP
.B \-?, \-\-help
Show the full help text.
.TP
.B \-\-usage
Show a short usage message.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the program version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NMCRCON_HOST
Default server host.
.TP
.B NMCRCON_PORT
Default server port.
.TP
.B NMCRCON_PASS
Default RCON password.
.TP
.B MCRCON_HOST, MCRCON_PORT, MCRCON_PASS
Compatibility fallbacks for Tiiffi/mcrcon environment variables.
.TP
.B NMCRCON_HISTORY
Path used to persist interactive command history.
.TP
.B NMCRCON_PS1
Interactive shell prompt string. The default prompt is
.BR "nmcrcon> " .
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B auth
Re-run authentication. An optional password may be provided as
.BR "auth PASSWORD" .
.TP
.B clear
Clear the screen.
.TP
.B connect [\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]]
Connect or reconnect to a server. When an argument is supplied it becomes the
new target endpoint.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect from the current server.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.TP
.B sleep \fISECONDS\fR
Pause execution for the given number of seconds.
.TP
.B source \fIFILE\fR
Execute commands from a script file.
.SH INTERACTIVE SHELL
The interactive shell is powered by
.BR bestline (3)
and supports history, prompt customization, shell shortcuts, and tab completion
for built-in commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B nmcrcon.1
This manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bestline (3)
